{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_47vat6uwz2kw2mbqmketphifzvotxmwowuv6asrjxjqigysymaka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All builds and tests pass. Here's a summary of the C-to-Rust translation:\n\n## Summary\n\n**`src/ulid.rs`** — Implemented `ulidgen_r`:\n- Sets the null terminator at index 26 (matching the C interface's `char[27]`).\n- Computes the current Unix timestamp in milliseconds and Crockford-Base32 encodes it into the first 10 chars of the ULID, tracking whether all positions are unchanged (`same`).\n- If `same`, increments the random portion in place: trailing `'Z'`s wrap to `'0'`, then the next char advances by one in the alphabet. If everything overflows, sleeps ~1.2 ms and recurses (matching the C behavior).\n- Otherwise generates 16 random bytes via `rand::thread_rng().fill_bytes` and encodes each into a Base32 char.\n\n**`src/ulidgen.rs`** — Implemented the `main` CLI:\n- Hand-rolled getopt-style parsing for `-n N` (with `-nN` and `-n N` forms) and `-t`.\n- `-t` mode: reads stdin lines, prints each prefixed with a freshly generated ULID, line-buffered.\n- Default mode: prints `n` ULIDs (default 1), one per line.\n- Returns 0 on success, 1 if a write fails.\n\n**`Cargo.toml`** — Added `rand = \"0.8\"` to replace the C `getentropy` call.\n\nThe remaining warnings are about pre-existing `use` statements in the source files (I cannot remove them without altering the originally-provided imports) and warnings in `src/bin/` files (which I'm not allowed to modify)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319,"cache_read_input_tokens":27949,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":319,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffde18ee-1808-40b4-b1fa-4e2565b7e12b","uuid":"c2bcf759-de37-4f74-b929-64d81f0